<title>USA: Most Ohio school ballot issues defeated by voters.</title>
<headline>Most Ohio school ballot issues defeated by voters.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Voters turned down most of the Ohio school levy and bond issue measures on Tuesday's ballot, according to the Ohio Department of Education.</p>
<p>The department reported that only nine out of 17 operating levy hikes were approved, while only two out of 11 bond issues passed. Voters also rejected three proposed capital levies.</p>
<p>((--Karen Pierog, 312-408-8647))</p>
